      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for lift-served skiing today, 9 September. The latest resort report describes superb snow conditions, with 0 cm overnight and in the last 24 hours, 7 cm over the last 7 days and a 140 cm natural snow base at the top of Home Basin. The grooming team has prepared an outstanding selection of freshly groomed trails for morning turns, while powder pockets remain higher on the mountain and the Saddle offers playful gullies. Current conditions are 1°C with 19 km/h winds and 34 km/h gusts, with a sunny start, increasing cloud later and snow forecast tonight. 3/3 lifts are open, with Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter operating. Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Motatapu Chutes, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access are all open. Groomed terrain includes Main Street, Roller Coaster, Upper & Lower Midwave, Raffil's Run, Side Saddle, Bullet, Saddleback, South Ridge & Wide Glide, and Pete's Treat & High Street. Home Basin is scheduled to open at 8:30 am, with Saddle Basin scheduled for 9:00 am. Today is a good day to hike the Summit Slopes, with Motatapu Chutes open. Visitors must enter terrain only through open gates and obey all closures. The access road is chain free, but all vehicles must carry chains, with a free shuttle operating from the bottom of the access road. An active road hazard advisory remains in place. The resort is also preparing for an action-packed weekend, including The Green Steam x POW Day x The Funk Royale on Saturday and the TC Interfields Ski Race on Sunday. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
